{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CghAf26L8tcA7p9QLwXuG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A line-item format change in **OrderService** reaches **5 services** within two hops.\n\n**Hop 1: depend on OrderService or call its API**\n1. **BillingService**: depends on OrderService.\n2. **ReportingService**: depends on OrderService.\n3. **SearchService**: depends on OrderService.\n4. **ApiGateway**: calls **OrdersAPI**, the API OrderService exposes. The graph treats a service and its API as one place, so this is one hop.\n\n**Hop 2: depend on the hop-1 services**\n5. **RenewalsWorker**: depends on BillingService, which depends on OrderService.\n\n**How I checked:** I ran a reverse-dependency query on OrderService over CALLS and DEPENDS_ON links, two hops deep. It returned these 5, well under the tool's 25-result cap, so nothing was cut off. I then queried ApiGateway, ReportingService and SearchService one hop deep each. Nothing depends on any of them, so RenewalsWorker is the only service at hop 2.\n\n**What this doesn't cover:** The query only follows CALLS and DEPENDS_ON links. It won't catch a service that reads OrderService's line items another way, such as straight from a database it stores in. It also can't tell which of these services actually read the line-item fields. BillingService and ReportingService seem the most likely to, and RenewalsWorker would only be affected if BillingService passes the change along. No configuration keys came up in this analysis."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 647, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4796, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 647}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "conte